9.2.1 Ensure 'Windows Firewall: Private: Firewall state' is set to 'On (recommended)' 


Navigate to the UI Path articulated in the Remediation section and confirm it is set as 
prescribed. This group policy setting is backed by the following registry location with a 
REG_DWORD value of 1. 


HKLM\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\WindowsFirewall\PrivateProfile:EnableFirewall 


Set-PolicyFileEntry -Path "$env:SystemRoot\System32\GroupPolicy\Machine\Registry.pol" -Key "SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\WindowsFirewall\PrivateProfile" -ValueName "EnableFirewall" -Data 1 -Type DWord -ErrorAction Stop


Get-PolicyFileEntry -Path "$env:SystemRoot\System32\GroupPolicy\Machine\Registry.pol" -Key "SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\WindowsFirewall\PrivateProfile" -ValueName "EnableFirewall"


gpupdate /target:computer /force


reg query "HKLM\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\WindowsFirewall\PrivateProfile" /v EnableFirewall


Get-ChildItem "$env:SystemRoot\System32\GroupPolicy" -Recurse -Force


gpedit.msc


Set-PolicyFileEntry -Path "$env:SystemRoot\System32\GroupPolicy\Machine\Registry.pol" -Key "SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\WindowsFirewall\DomainProfile" -ValueName "EnableFirewall" -Data 1 -Type DWord -ErrorAction Stop


Get-PolicyFileEntry -Path "$env:SystemRoot\System32\GroupPolicy\Machine\Registry.pol" -Key "SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\WindowsFirewall\DomainProfile" -ValueName "EnableFirewall"


gpupdate /force


reg query "HKLM\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\WindowsFirewall\DomainProfile" /v EnableFirewall


Set-ItemProperty -Path "HKCU:\Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Applets\Regedit" -Name LastKey -Value "Computer\HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\WindowsFirewall\DomainProfile"; Start-Process regedit.exe


